{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-chirality-writhe-ribbon-derivation","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:chirality-writhe-ribbon-derivation","kind":"proposition","title":"Chirality factor $1 + w \\cdot h$ from ribbon-twist framing (writhe $w$)","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-e-infinity-page-identifications"],"tags":["chirality","writhe","ribbon","kauffman-framing","derivation","term-5"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.chirality_writhe_ribbon","text":"chirality-writhe-ribbon-derivation.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:chirality-writhe-ribbon-derivation\"></a><p><em>For a braid <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\beta</code> with integer writhe <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">w(\\beta)</code>, the chirality factor derived from the Kauffman ribbon-twist evaluation limits strictly to:</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  a_K(\\beta)\n  \\;=\\;\n  1 \\;+\\; w(\\beta) \\cdot h \\;+\\; O(h^2).</code></pre>\n<p>The first-order Hecke deformation factor is therefore fixed by the topological writhe.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/chirality-writhe-ribbon-derivation.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"13.26.11","page":"b/prop-chirality-writhe-ribbon-derivation","qa":{"counts":{"pass":87,"fail":2,"warn":0,"na":12,"unknown":0,"stale":74},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ChiralityWritheRibbon.chirality_writhe_ribbon","via":"ref","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ChiralityWritheRibbon.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
